WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.512
The clicking, typing, and copying you still do by hand.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.764
RPA promised to take it off you.

00:00:08.764 --> 00:00:11.017
But every robot was built by hand,

00:00:11.017 --> 00:00:14.180
and fixed by hand whenever a screen changed.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.456
Now AI builds it.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.267
Describe the job,

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.870
and Kitewell lays out every step for you to check.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.172
Or build it from Claude Code or Codex, over MCP.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.897
On the first run, AI learns the job in your browser.

00:00:29.897 --> 00:00:32.112
Then your computer runs it, every day.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.676
When a site changes, AI finds the new way, and keeps it.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.375
It stops for your OK where it matters.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.333
Got a list in Excel?

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.900
It runs every row and writes the results back.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.314
Coding agents too.

00:00:46.314 --> 00:00:49.876
Claude Code writes the fix, Codex reviews it,

00:00:49.876 --> 00:00:52.150
and nothing ships until you approve.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.708
It runs on your computer, and your passwords stay there.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:59.443
Run it on every computer, and watch them all from the cloud.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.726
If a run fails, or a computer goes quiet, you hear about it.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.410
Kitewell.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.160
It flies on its own.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.456
You hold the string.
